text:
anna: Heads-up — on iPhone SE (320px) the left rail overlaps row action buttons in Runs table, so you can’t tap the actions reliably.

mike: saw that — can you paste repro steps?

anna: Console > Projects > select a project with many runs. Narrow viewport, open row menu or try swipe-to-reveal actions — the collapsed sidebar sits above the row content. Screenshot: https://redwood-internal/figures/320px-rail-overlap.png

sam: also noticed the chevron hit area is ~28px on that page, we should bump to 44px minimum for touch.

jess: +1. Options: 1) make sidebar a full-screen drawer under 360px, 2) move row actions into a kebab overflow on narrow widths, 3) sticky bottom action bar (but may conflict with keyboard).

will: personally prefer overflow menu to avoid blocking content. Drawer works too if we trap focus correctly.

anna: Mock in Figma: https://www.figma.com/file/AbCdEf/console-responsive — proposal: drawer at <=360px, icon-only rail at 361-420 with labels hidden, increase hit targets.

mike: Drawer + aria labels for icon-only buttons sounds good. Don’t forget visible focus outline for keyboard users.

sam: quick CSS I used to prototype touch area fix:
```
.table-row .chevron { padding: 8px; touch-action: manipulation; }
@media (max-width: 420px) {
  .sidebar { position: fixed; inset: 0 0 0 0; transform: translateX(-100%); /* hidden by default, slide in */ }
  .row-actions { display: none; }
  .row-overflow { display: inline-block; }
}
```
jess: can we add a Percy visual test for 320/375/420 width snapshots so regressions show up?

deploy-bot: Percy snapshot created: build/4823/narrow-sidebar-320.png ✅

anna: OK I’ll update the PR: implement drawer breakpoint, add aria-labels to icon-only controls, bump chevron padding, and add Percy snapshots. Assigning review to @sam for accessibility check.

sam: I’ll review tomorrow AM. Quick a11y notes: ensure drawer traps keyboard focus, Esc closes it, and icon buttons have aria-label + visible label in screen reader text.

mike: moving to design review board. :thumbsup:
